# Growth engine (slide.relentless)

Workdir: `growth-engine/`. Live dashboard: https://slide.remedyrecoveries.com
Cloudflare Pages project: `remedy-growth`. Production branch: `main`.

## Deploy (always `npm run deploy` — never raw wrangler)

```powershell
cd growth-engine
npm run deploy
```

That script builds the dashboard and deploys with `--branch=main`. Do not stop at a local preview. Do **not** run `npx wrangler pages deploy` yourself.

### Why edits sometimes "don't go through"

`wrangler pages deploy` **without** `--branch=main` defaults to git branch `master` → Cloudflare **Preview**. The custom domain `slide.remedyrecoveries.com` only serves the **Production** environment (branch `main`). Preview deploys succeed and print a `*.pages.dev` URL, but the live site does not change.

If a deploy just ran and the live site looks stale:

1. Confirm the command was `npm run deploy` (or wrangler with `--branch=main`). If it was raw wrangler without that flag, the update is on Preview only — redeploy with `npm run deploy`.
2. Hard-refresh https://slide.remedyrecoveries.com (cache can hide a real production deploy).

