## Screenshots — library crops only (no shortcuts)

User-made `crop_*.png` files (and anything with `cropped: true` in `meta.json`) are **protected**.

- **Do not delete them.** Not in a cleanup, reset, “system crop”, or “ones I made” pass.
- Do not add them to `library-overrides.json` `deletedScreenshots`.
- Do not call `DELETE /api/assets/screenshots/:file` on a `crop_*` file unless the user names **that exact filename** in the same message.
- After the 2026-08-24 wipe, the user re-saved these crops. Keep them: `crop_cat_cow`, `crop_home`, `crop_home_2`, `crop_img_0461`, `crop_img_0462`, `crop_img_0462_2`, `crop_img_0462_4`, `crop_img_0465`, `crop_img_0469`, `crop_img_0470`, `crop_img_0472`, `crop_img_0473`, `crop_pain_check`, `crop_profile`, `crop_progress`, `crop_progress_2`, `crop_progress_3`, `crop_session`, `crop_session_preview`.

**Never invent a crop.** Do not `sharp.extract`, write a new `crop_*.png`, or invent `skipTopPct` / `cropHPct` to “fix” a slide. The only way a new crop enters the library is the Images **Crop** tab / `POST /api/assets/crop-requests/:id/fulfill` (Rahul uploads the crop). If no library crop fits, say so and stop — do not assign a raw `img_*.png` / full screenshot (those get a generic 45% top slice and look cut off). Generate may only attach files from `listAssignableScreenshots()` (crops only).

